    <item>
      <title>Hangout #55 | 10 YEARS of Startup Portugal - Lisboa &amp; Porto</title>
      <link>https://luma.com/9u7ixau4?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1207</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 09:14:33 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>Ferroviário (Rua de Santa Apolónia 59, 1100-468 Lisboa)
+
Edifício Transparente (Via do Castelo do Queijo 335 419, 4100-429 Porto)
+
ONLINE (via Zoom)

Ten years ago, Startup Portugal set out to help build a stronger, more connected startup ecosystem. In this special anniversary Hangout, we&apos;ll look back at what has been achieved along the way: the programs, the policies, the communities, and the founders that shaped a decade of Portuguese entrepreneurship.
But this is not just a celebration of t</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=1,anim=false,background=white,quality=75,width=800,height=420/event-social/zf/cfeeb799-91be-4190-832b-611d8c4cd8c3.png" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Wednesday, 30 September 2026 at 17:30<br><strong>Where:</strong> Porto</p><p>Ferroviário (Rua de Santa Apolónia 59, 1100-468 Lisboa)<br>+<br>Edifício Transparente (Via do Castelo do Queijo 335 419, 4100-429 Porto)<br>+<br>ONLINE (via Zoom)<br><br>Ten years ago, Startup Portugal set out to help build a stronger, more connected startup ecosystem. In this special anniversary Hangout, we&apos;ll look back at what has been achieved along the way: the programs, the policies, the communities, and the founders that shaped a decade of Portuguese entrepreneurship.<br>But this is not just a celebration of the past. Showing what we want for the next 10 years, we&apos;ll also look ahead at where the ecosystem is going and what it will take to keep building something bigger, more robust, and more resilient. Whether you&apos;ve been part of this journey from day one or just joined the ride, come celebrate with us and help shape the next chapter.<br><br>Connect before you arrive<br>The community has a space on Meetball. Before the event, see what people are working on and what they need help with. Post what you&apos;re looking for. Show up already knowing who to talk to.<br>👉 Join the Startup Portugal space on Meetball: https://app.meetball.fun/communities/startup-portugal</p><p><a href="https://luma.com/9u7ixau4?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Finnovation Night@SBC Summit - Payments × Gaming: Building the Financial Infrastructure Behind iGaming</title>
      <link>https://luma.com/wz2osut7?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1236</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 11:59:27 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>Hey Lisbon, get ready for a night of curated networking, drinks, music, and high-energy connections - with expert conversations and a FinTech × Gaming Innovation Showcase alongside SBC Summit.
Finnovation Night: Payments × Gaming brings together gaming operators, payment providers, fintech companies, fraud, risk and compliance leaders, and technology innovators shaping the financial infrastructure behind iGaming.
Hosted by Svitlanka Serhiichuk, FinTech Ambassador at TechEmbassy and Co-Founder of</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=1,anim=false,background=white,quality=75,width=800,height=420/event-social/ew/3d3e9ad7-3450-4180-886b-1f3029311fc6.png" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Wednesday, 30 September 2026 at 18:00<br><strong>Where:</strong> Lisboa</p><p>Hey Lisbon, get ready for a night of curated networking, drinks, music, and high-energy connections - with expert conversations and a FinTech × Gaming Innovation Showcase alongside SBC Summit.<br>Finnovation Night: Payments × Gaming brings together gaming operators, payment providers, fintech companies, fraud, risk and compliance leaders, and technology innovators shaping the financial infrastructure behind iGaming.<br>Hosted by Svitlanka Serhiichuk, FinTech Ambassador at TechEmbassy and Co-Founder of Neofin.<br>Organized in partnership with Future Finance Fest (3F), a global community connecting internationally recognized fintech scholars, policy experts and industry executives to bridge academic research with real-world financial innovation.<br>What to Expect<br>🎤 Expert Conversations<br>Industry leaders discussing payments, conversion, fraud, identity, compliance and the future of financial infrastructure in gaming.<br>⚡ FinTech × Gaming Innovation Showcase<br>A short showcase featuring up to three selected products and technologies changing how money and identity move through the gaming ecosystem.<br>🤝 Curated Networking<br>Meet gaming operators, PSPs, acquirers, payment and infrastructure companies, fraud and identity providers, compliance and risk leaders, and other decision-makers during SBC week.<br>From Business to Party<br>The night starts with focused industry conversations and curated networking — and as the programme wraps up, the atmosphere shifts.<br>Stay for drinks, music, DJs and Finnovation Night &amp; Party — a chance to keep the conversations going, make new connections and enjoy the night beyond the conference floor.<br>Think of it as Finnovation Day after dark: expert content first, business connections next, party afterwards.<br>🎙 Speakers<br>Coming soon.<br>🤝 Partners<br>Finnovation Night is made possible through collaboration with our ecosystem partners, sponsors and local fintech communities.<br>📍 Where the Night Happens - The Station by SEXTO<br>We’re taking over The Station by SEXTO, a two-level Lisbon venue with multiple spaces for conversations, drinks, music and dancing.<br><br>About TechEmbassy<br>TechEmbassy builds curated communities around the world&apos;s leading technology conferences, creating meaningful connections between founders, enterprises, investors and industry experts.<br>Through the Finnovation Day series, we bring together the people shaping modern financial services, from banks and payment companies to infrastructure providers, regulators and researchers, for conversations that continue long after the conference week ends.<br>Finnovation Night Lisbon is one stop in our Global Series — explore the full calendar of our events around the world at https://techembassy.org/<br>🌐 Website: https://techembassy.org/<br>📅 Events calendar: https://luma.com/techembassy.org<br>💼 LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/company/tech-embassy/</p><p><a href="https://luma.com/wz2osut7?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Storytelling Night—&quot;EXES&quot;</title>
      <link>https://luma.com/uoidxmew?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1256</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:57:09 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>Our theme for September is EXES.
The people we left. People who left us. People who were once there and now are not.
Maybe it&apos;s the night you met your ex-therapist in a bar, or the day your ex-boss called to ask you out.
As always, interpret the theme freely.
Give us stories of former friends, bosses, roommates or lovers. Clean breaks and messy endings. Exes who disappeared and exes who reappeared.
Please come just to listen or get on stage, be vulnerable, and share with us, a diverse group of w</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=1,anim=false,background=white,quality=75,width=800,height=420/event-social/4d/73632aed-1d7c-425f-b7b8-cbcc0921a8e3.png" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Wednesday, 30 September 2026 at 19:30<br><strong>Where:</strong> Lisboa</p><p>Our theme for September is EXES.<br>The people we left. People who left us. People who were once there and now are not.<br>Maybe it&apos;s the night you met your ex-therapist in a bar, or the day your ex-boss called to ask you out.<br>As always, interpret the theme freely.<br>Give us stories of former friends, bosses, roommates or lovers. Clean breaks and messy endings. Exes who disappeared and exes who reappeared.<br>Please come just to listen or get on stage, be vulnerable, and share with us, a diverse group of welcoming and open people who are curious about each others&apos; lives.<br>Stories will last from 7 to 10 minutes. Expect ten stories plus an intermission.<br>We hold our event at Fábrica Braço de Prata, an enormous multi-roomed centro cultural in Marvila that hosts everything from salsa bands to intimate piano concerts to philosophical comedy.<br>To accommodate everyone, we will be in the outdoor tent right inside the gate to Fábrica Braço de Prata. Love is a popular edition, arrive early to get good seats.<br>Storytelling Lisboa is a completely free event run by volunteers. We welcome everyone to get on stage!<br>Absolutely no experience is necessary.We only ask that stories be true and personal and that they are performed as opposed to read—and they should be stories instead of philosophical musings, motivational speeches, or stand-up routines.The content is completely at the discretion of the storyteller as long as it is related in the monthly theme and respectful to the diversity and experiences of all humans.<br>Interested in sharing a story? We give spots on a first come, first serve basis. We want all voices! Please fill out our sign-up form here: https://forms.gle/kkGhEM47BLF4WRkg9<br>We now have an email list and WhatsApp group to subscribe to to keep up with events. You can sign up for either of these via our linktree: https://linktr.ee/storytellinglisboa<br>For any questions, you can reach out to us by DM on our instagram @storytellinglisboa! Or email storytellinglisboa at gmail dot com.<br>Bring some cash to throw into our donation jar! We will always be free and want everyone to be able to attend, but your funds help sustain the increasing effort and volunteers needed to put on the event.</p><p><a href="https://luma.com/uoidxmew?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>P.S. Lisbon</title>
      <link>https://luma.com/P.S.Lisbon?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1197</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 21:53:56 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>Lisbon has always been a city for the people who explore and build. Following that same spirit, INPUT, Paybis  and Nsure.ai are bringing together the founders, investors and operators reshaping iGaming and payments, for an evening in Alfama, the oldest neighbourhood in Lisbon.
October 1st, at La Distillerie, a 19th century distillery at the heart of the neighbourhood. Music, Portuguese wine, and the kind of company worth writing home about.

What to expect
Founders, investors, and leaders from a</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=1,anim=false,background=white,quality=75,width=800,height=420/event-social/1h/d760b2d2-d753-4e8d-8314-3825869b8e2f.png" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Thursday, 1 October 2026 at 18:00<br><strong>Where:</strong> Lisboa</p><p>Lisbon has always been a city for the people who explore and build. Following that same spirit, INPUT, Paybis  and Nsure.ai are bringing together the founders, investors and operators reshaping iGaming and payments, for an evening in Alfama, the oldest neighbourhood in Lisbon.<br>October 1st, at La Distillerie, a 19th century distillery at the heart of the neighbourhood. Music, Portuguese wine, and the kind of company worth writing home about.<br><br>What to expect<br>Founders, investors, and leaders from across iGaming and payments<br>Portuguese wine tasting led by a sommelier<br>Cocktails and canapés throughout<br>DJ set through the night<br>Postcard Corner: pick a card, write something worth sending, and drop it in the box. It gets stamped and mailed straight to your door.<br>A relaxed evening, no agenda, no panels, just good company<br><br>The venue<br>La Distillerie sits at the heart of Alfama, Lisbon&apos;s oldest neighbourhood. A 19th century distillery, high ceilings, stone walls, authentic Portuguese details.<br><br>Co-hosted by Paybis<br>Paybis makes crypto simple for individuals and enterprises. Established in 2014, the company combines a trusted crypto exchange and wallet—to buy, sell, swap and hold over 90 cryptocurrencies—with award-winning crypto-fiat infrastructure. This infrastructure empowers businesses to transfer capital globally, eliminating traditional payment friction.<br>In 2026, Paybis was recognized as the Best Crypto Payment Provider, a testament to our expansive global reach, rapid onboarding protocols, and the deep expertise of the 200 dedicated professionals who drive our operations.<br>Processing more than $6bn annually, Paybis is one of the most efficient platforms for acquiring and transacting in digital assets. This commitment to operational excellence is why Paybis maintains one of the highest ratings for crypto companies on Trustpilot, and why 7 million users and hundreds of the world&apos;s fastest-growing enterprises consistently rely on our services.<br>X | LinkedIn | Website | YouTube<br><br>Co-hosted by nSure.ai<br>nSure.ai is an AI-native payment fraud prevention solution that turns risk management into a scalable growth engine. It serves crypto exchanges, digital asset platforms, fintechs, stablecoin PSPs, remittance providers, iGaming operators, and prepaid platforms (incl. gift cards), empowering high-risk merchants to maximize net incremental profit by removing payment friction and false declines.<br>Instead of static rules or shared pooled models, nSure.ai builds a dedicated AI model for every merchant, trained on their unique transaction data to isolate legitimate buyer behavior. Backed by a 100% financial liability shift (chargeback guarantee), the platform approves more valid customers to deliver approval rates up to 98%.<br>Processing over $200B in annual volume, nSure.ai is one of the most scalable fraud engines in digital commerce. Rendering decisions under 500ms and handling peak volumes of $80M/hr, nSure.ai’s operational excellence has driven 3x YoY growth while safeguarding leading global enterprises.<br>LinkedIn | Website<br><br>Powered by INPUT Global<br>INPUT  - global communications partner for emerging tech companies and founders. We help companies earn market legitimacy and founder visibility through broader communications.<br><br>How we do it:<br>• PR – authority and visibility through Tier-1 media<br>• Personal branding – making founders’ Voice™ known<br>• Influencers – performance-driven campaigns<br>• Events – speaking on stage or hosting your own.<br><br>Who we work with:<br>For Fintech, Crypto, AI and iGaming companies.<br>Where our communications go broader:<br>Across the Americas, Europe, Asia, and MENA.<br><br>Track record:<br>• 500+ companies and leadership teams have worked with INPUT<br>• including CBI, Tether, Ledger, 1win, TRON, Bitget, and Outlier Ventures<br>• 90% of our clients stay with us year by year.<br>X | LinkedIn | Website</p><p><a href="https://luma.com/P.S.Lisbon?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
