    <item>
      <title>RedBridge Lisbon - #SFTechWeek</title>
      <link>https://partiful.com/e/XDQjzJRlWFiGQQOwrmHg?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1238</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 13:44:37 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>RedBridge Demo &amp; Connect: The Gateway to Portugal&apos;s Innovation Ecosystem

Portugal&apos;s startup ecosystem is emerging as one of Europe&apos;s most exciting innovation stories.
Home to globally recognized startups, multiple unicorns, a thriving founder community, and one of Europe&apos;s fastest-growing technology hubs, Portugal is increasingly attracting entrepreneurs, investors, and companies looking to build globally.

An evening bringing together founders, investors, operators, and ecosystem leaders from </description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://partiful.imgix.net/external/user/ATRlsFElgDcYDGVH8KKZSZyeUsn2/OEKhs94GSoCzKn4dlGjrY?w=1000&amp;h=1000&amp;fit=clip" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Wednesday, 7 October 2026 at 01:30<br><strong>Where:</strong> Lisboa</p><p>RedBridge Demo &amp; Connect: The Gateway to Portugal&apos;s Innovation Ecosystem<br><br>Portugal&apos;s startup ecosystem is emerging as one of Europe&apos;s most exciting innovation stories.<br>Home to globally recognized startups, multiple unicorns, a thriving founder community, and one of Europe&apos;s fastest-growing technology hubs, Portugal is increasingly attracting entrepreneurs, investors, and companies looking to build globally.<br><br>An evening bringing together founders, investors, operators, and ecosystem leaders from Portugal and Silicon Valley.<br><br>The event is part of Portugal at SF Tech Week, a curated Silicon Valley access program organized by RedBridge Lisbon, in collaboration with Unicorn Factory Lisbon and Startup Portugal, supported by the Consulate General of Portugal in San Francisco and AICEP San Francisco, with ecosystem partner THV.<br><br>It also marks an important milestone in the broader Lisbon–San Francisco Innovation Bridge, an initiative designed to strengthen long-term collaboration between two leading innovation ecosystems.<br><br>Throughout the week, a carefully selected cohort of Portuguese startups is participating in a curated program across Silicon Valley, meeting leading venture capital firms, accelerators, founders, and operators. <br><br>RedBridge Demo &amp; Connect is the moment when the SF Tech Week community can meet these founders, discover their companies, and connect with the organizations shaping Portugal&apos;s innovation ecosystem.<br><br>The evening will feature opening remarks and insights from Filipe Ramalheira, Consul General of Portugal in San Francisco, the participation of Pedro Macedo Leão, Head of AICEP San Francisco, and a fireside chat with leaders from Startup Portugal and Unicorn Factory Lisbon, discussing why Portugal has become one of Europe&apos;s most dynamic destinations for innovation and entrepreneurship.<br><br>Whether you&apos;re looking for investment opportunities, international partnerships, exceptional founders, or simply want to understand why Portugal is increasingly on the radar of global technology companies and investors, this is an evening designed to spark meaningful conversations and lasting connections.<br><br>Come discover what&apos;s happening in Portugal—and meet the founders building what&apos;s next.<br><br>5:30 PM — Doors Open &amp; Welcome Reception<br>Guests arrive for networking, drinks, and informal introductions with founders, investors, operators, and members of the Bay Area innovation community.<br><br>6:00 PM — Opening Remarks<br>Welcome by RedBridge.<br>Opening remarks by:<br> Filipe Ramalheira, Consul General of Portugal in San Francisco<br><br>6:10 PM — Fireside Chat<br>Portugal&apos;s Breakout Moment<br>Speakers<br> Miguel Aguiar, Executive Director, Startup Portugal<br> Gil Azevedo, Executive Director, Unicorn Factory Lisboa<br><br>Moderator<br> Neil Cohen, Head of Marketing Portal 26, RedBridge Board Member<br><br>A 15-minute conversation exploring Portugal&apos;s rise as one of Europe&apos;s most dynamic innovation ecosystems, its momentum in entrepreneurship, venture investment, and technology, and the opportunities for founders, investors, and companies building across both sides of the Atlantic.<br><br>6:25 PM — Startup Showcase<br>Ten Portuguese startups selected for Portugal at SF Tech Week will each deliver a 3-minute pitch, showcasing innovative solutions across multiple sectors and sharing their vision for global growth.<br>Meet some of Portugal&apos;s most promising founders and discover the next generation of globally ambitious startups emerging from the Portuguese ecosystem.<br><br>7:00 PM – 8:00 PM — Networking Reception<br>Continue the conversation over drinks with founders, investors, operators, corporates, and members of the Bay Area innovation community.<br>Explore investment opportunities, discuss partnerships, and build new connections between Silicon Valley and Portugal<br><br>This event is a part of #SFTechWeek—a week of events hosted by VCs and startups to bring together the tech ecosystem. Learn more at www.tech-week.com.</p><p><a href="https://partiful.com/e/XDQjzJRlWFiGQQOwrmHg?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
