    <item>
      <title>An evening with Nir Eyal — Belief as competitive edge</title>
      <link>https://luma.com/nir-eyal-lisbon?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1218</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 06 Sep 2026 19:03:10 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>What we believe affects what we notice, the decisions we make, and what we think is possible.
Join us in Lisbon for a special evening with Nir Eyal, behavioral design expert and author of the New York Times bestseller Beyond Belief, as well as the international bestsellers Indistractable and Hooked.
In Hooked, Nir explored how products create habits. In Indistractable, he showed how we can take control of our attention. His latest book, Beyond Belief, looks at something even deeper: how hidden a</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=1,anim=false,background=white,quality=75,width=800,height=420/event-social/qj/dd7cdffe-b1ec-486c-b5f8-45115b86f828.png" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Thursday, 22 October 2026 at 18:00<br><strong>Where:</strong> Lisboa</p><p>What we believe affects what we notice, the decisions we make, and what we think is possible.<br>Join us in Lisbon for a special evening with Nir Eyal, behavioral design expert and author of the New York Times bestseller Beyond Belief, as well as the international bestsellers Indistractable and Hooked.<br>In Hooked, Nir explored how products create habits. In Indistractable, he showed how we can take control of our attention. His latest book, Beyond Belief, looks at something even deeper: how hidden assumptions influence our behavior, performance, and potential.<br>During his keynote, Nir will share how we can identify the beliefs holding us back, question the stories we tell ourselves, and develop beliefs that help us move forward.<br><br>What you will learn<br>How beliefs influence our actions and decisions<br>Why limiting beliefs can feel like objective facts<br>How to challenge assumptions that hold us back<br>How attention, habits, and beliefs work together<br>Practical ways to improve performance without relying only on motivation<br><br>Agenda<br>6:00 PM | Doors open &amp; informal networking<br>Arrive, grab a drink, and connect with fellow founders, leaders, product people, and professionals from different industries.<br>6:20 PM | Official welcome<br>A short introduction to the evening and what to expect.<br>6:30 PM | Keynote with Nir Eyal<br>A 45-minute keynote exploring how our beliefs influence our focus, decisions, performance, and what we believe is possible.<br>7:15 PM | Fireside chat &amp; audience Q&amp;A<br>Around 40 minutes of conversation with Nir, followed by questions from the audience.<br>8:00 PM–10:00 PM | Networking, drinks &amp; conversations<br>Continue the evening with informal conversations, new connections, and time to meet Nir and other guests.<br><br>Who is this for?<br>This event is for:<br>Founders and entrepreneurs<br>Business and team leaders<br>Product, innovation, and technology professionals<br>Creators and independent professionals<br>People interested in behavioral science and personal development<br>Anyone who wants to improve their focus, confidence, and performance</p><p><a href="https://luma.com/nir-eyal-lisbon?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>SPACE X AI -  </title>
      <link>https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScPxbkrmWQKIu7iOFXr1exw3jKMPA7XFBFq8vMhZxZNGcJD3A/viewform?usp=embed_facebook&amp;utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1263</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:23:38 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>Participation is free 
Nos dias 26 e 27 de outubro, o Laboratório de IA e Transformação Digital SpaceXAI reúne, no Forum Braga, PME portuguesas, especialistas e ferramentas de Inteligência Artificial num formato intensivo e prático, concebido para acelerar a adoção destas tecnologias pelas empresas.

Cada empresa participante irá trabalhar sobre um desafio real da sua organização, com o acompanhamento de especialistas e acesso a ferramentas de IA, procurando transformar esse problema numa soluçã</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/10Wtqf2x2EZjpvZoum5012GAwquQB8YnD54PDpVIxkd2-kgfY2a5R1OYH8LxAKCLPnEQaUTD7UyJTR0=w1200-h630-p" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Monday, 26 October 2026 at 09:00<br><strong>Where:</strong> Braga</p><p>Participation is free <br>Nos dias 26 e 27 de outubro, o Laboratório de IA e Transformação Digital SpaceXAI reúne, no Forum Braga, PME portuguesas, especialistas e ferramentas de Inteligência Artificial num formato intensivo e prático, concebido para acelerar a adoção destas tecnologias pelas empresas.<br><br>Cada empresa participante irá trabalhar sobre um desafio real da sua organização, com o acompanhamento de especialistas e acesso a ferramentas de IA, procurando transformar esse problema numa solução, protótipo ou workflow com potencial de aplicação efetiva na empresa.<br><br>Não é uma conferência sobre Inteligência Artificial. É um espaço para experimentar, desenvolver e aplicar IA a problemas concretos das PME.<br><br>Na iniciativa da SpaceXAI, os participantes terão acesso a sessões de mentoria, bem como a toda a componente técnica do Laboratório assegurada por aquela empresa, incluindo as ferramentas, as sessões práticas e o acompanhamento especializado das equipas durante os dois dias.<br><br>A participação é gratuita, mediante candidatura e seleção.<br><br> </p><p><a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScPxbkrmWQKIu7iOFXr1exw3jKMPA7XFBFq8vMhZxZNGcJD3A/viewform?usp=embed_facebook&amp;utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_startups-fundraising">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
